e3.0/tmp8no4_fk1.prompt","content":"- **ask_human(question, options?, urgent?)** — Escalate to human when you cannot make a decision. Use sparingly.\n- **notify_human(message, level)** — Inform human of significant events (all tasks done, critical failure, etc.)\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Do NOT guess when unsure — use `escalate`\n- Do NOT approve merges without reviewing the diff summary\n- Do NOT create tasks with vague prompts — workers have zero context beyond what you write\n- Do NOT retry indefinitely — respect max_attempts\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\n{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: Add tests in tests/ directory following existing patterns.\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The session-protocol spec itself - only implement the missing commands it references.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:24:35.941449\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472034, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n{\"id\": \"task-002\", \"branch\": \"collab/spec-purpose-updates\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/spec-purpose-updates\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Fill in TBD Purpose fields for three specs\", \"prompt\": \"Update the Purpose fields for three specs that currently have \\\"TBD - created by archiving change\\\" placeholders.\\n\\n**Specs to update**:\\n1. **spec-lint** (openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n2. **requirement-intake** (openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change requirement-capture. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n3. **change-verifier** (openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n\\n**How to determine the Purpose**:\\nRead each spec's Requirements section and understand what it governs. Write a clear 1-2 sentence Purpose that explains:\\n- What this spec defines/controls\\n- Why it exists in the SE3 framework\\n\\n**Example good Purpose** (from session-protocol):\\n\\\"Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup, execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\\\"\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n\\n**What to edit**:\\nOnly update the \\\"## Purpose\\\" section in each of the three spec files. Do not change any other content.\\n\\n**Verification**: Run `se3 lint` after changes to ensure specs are still valid.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:35:59.691789\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472064, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-003\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-calls-archive\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-calls-archive\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement human calls archiving system\", \"prompt\": \"Implement an archiving system for completed human calls.\\n\\n**Background**: The human-as-mcp spec defines async human calls stored in `human-calls/` directory. Currently there's no system to archive completed calls - they just accumulate in the main directory.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-calls/archive/` directory structure\\n2. Add `se3 human-calls archive` command that:\\n   - Moves completed human calls (those with Response sections filled) to human-calls/archive/\\n   - Preserves the original filename format: `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{description}.md`\\n   - Optionally supports `--dry-run` to preview what would be archived\\n3. Add `se3 human-calls list` command that:\\n   - Lists pending (unresponded) human calls\\n   - Lists recently archived calls\\n4. Update `se3 collab --status` to show pending human calls count (mentioned in issues.md)\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand human call format)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing human call utilities)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py (see how --status works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/status.py (for reference on status display)\\n\\n**Human call file format**:\\nFiles in human-calls/ have Request and Response sections. A call is \\\"completed\\\" when the Response section has content.\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- Add the new commands to tools/se3_tools/commands/ (create human_calls.py or similar)\\n- Register commands in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI output and error handling\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec itself - only implement the archiving functionality.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:40:26.290942\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2475858, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n{\"id\": \"task-004\", \"branch\": \"collab/remove-external-controller\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/remove-external-controller\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Remove deprecated se3-controller spec\", \"prompt\": \"Remove or archive the deprecated se3-controller spec.\\n\\n**Background**: The git-worktree-collab spec (v2) explicitly removed the External Controller architecture. The se3-controller spec is marked as experimental and deprecated. The git-worktree-collab spec states:\\n- \\\"Replace the experimental External Controller (v2)\\\"\\n- Lists REMOVED items: \\\"Python daemon process\\\", \\\"HTTP API server\\\", \\\"MCP server for manager-worker communication\\\"\\n\\n**What to do**:\\n1. Read the EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md in openspec/specs/se3-controller/ to understand what it documented\\n2. Archive the se3-controller spec to openspec/changes/archive/ (similar to other archived changes)\\n3. Create an archive entry documenting that this was removed in favor of git-worktree-collab\\n4. Remove the se3-controller directory from openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md (lines 30-45 for removal rationale)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml (the OpenAPI spec)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md\\n- openspec/changes/archive/ (see how other changes are archived for reference)\\n\\n**Archive format**:\\nFollow the pattern in openspec/changes/archive/:\\n- Create directory openspec/changes/archive/remove-se3-controller/\\n- Move the spec files there\\n- Add a CHANGE.md explaining why it was removed and what replaced it\\n\\n**Verification**: Ensure `se3 lint` still passes after removal.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:30:23.879988\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2475888, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-005\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-input-methods\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-input-methods\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement file-based human input method\", \"prompt\": \"Implement support for human input via prompt files as an alternative to MCP calls.\\n\\n**Background**: issues.md mentions: \\\"human\\u4ece\\u4ea4\\u4e92\\u754c\\u9762\\u4e4b\\u5916\\u7684\\u8f93\\u5165\\u65b9\\u5f0f\\uff0c\\u4ee5\\u53ca\\u8f93\\u5165\\u7684\\u5f52\\u6863\\\" (human input methods outside the interaction interface, and archiving of such input). This refers to supporting file-based human input in addition to sync/async MCP calls.\\n\